<title>CANADA: Canada May bankruptcies rise over year.</title>
<headline>Canada May bankruptcies rise over year.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankruptcies in Canada rose to 8,677 in May from 8,379 a year earlier, the Department of Consumer and Corporate Affairs said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The department said 1,055 businesses and 7,622 consumers went bankrupt in the month.</p>
<p>In April, 9,703 bankruptcies were recorded.</p>
<p>For the year to date, 42,868 bankruptcies have been registered (5,581 businesses and 37,287 consumers), up from 39,560 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
